    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d157-a1">

                <pb facs="0384" n="288" sameAs="frus:frus1879/pg288"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 96.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Dichman to Mr.
                            Rico.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Bogota</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-06-03"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 3,
                        1879</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Information has reached this legation that
                    the government of the State of Tolima has issued a decree declaring public order
                    in danger of being disturbed, and under this novel expedient it is proposed to
                    levy and collect a tax for war purposes, among others, from citizens of the
                    United States.</p>
                <p>Without endeavoring to discuss the merits of this question, I beg to bring these
                    facts to your notice in order that you may be pleased to take such steps in
                    relation thereto as may be in conformity with the laws and treaties on this
                    subject.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>ERNEST DICHMAN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
